# On a server host, this repository IS the installation directory: config/ and
# log/ live inside the checkout (see scripts/config.sh — HOST_CONFIG_BASE and
# HOST_LOG_BASE are derived from the repository root). Runtime state therefore
# appears right next to tracked files, and a careless `git add -A` in an
# installation directory would commit it.
#
# Everything below is generated at runtime and belongs to one specific host.
# None of it should ever be committed.

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The server's SSH host key pair, generated by entrypoint.sh on first start and
# persisted here so the server's identity survives container restarts. The
# private half is what clients pin when they accept the host fingerprint;
# publishing it would let anyone impersonate this server to its own clients.
config/ssh_host_keys/

# --- Per-host configuration --------------------------------------------------
#
# The client roster: names, groups, repository paths and quotas. The public
# keys themselves are not secret, but the list of who is backed up and how much
# they are allowed to store usually is.
config/clients.conf
config/keys/

# --- Generated systemd artifacts ---------------------------------------------
#
# snapshots/71-timer-install.sh and scripts/21-check-timer-install.sh render
# their .service unit from a template with this checkout's own REPO_ROOT baked
# into ExecStart — valid on exactly one machine.
#
# (The Borg container's own unit no longer renders anything: it is a Podman
# Quadlet, installed by 50-service-install.sh under
# ~/.config/containers/systemd/ with a generated 10-deployment.conf drop-in —
# both outside the checkout, so there is nothing here to ignore for it.)
snapshots/*.rendered
scripts/*.rendered

# --- Runtime logs ------------------------------------------------------------
log/

# --- Editor and OS noise -----------------------------------------------------
*~
*.swp
.DS_Store

# --- German test reports & lab notes ----------------------------------------
#
# The maintainer's verification material — per-release Prüfberichte, pentest /
# audit reports, and the concrete test-VM inventory (TESTLAB.md) — is
# German-language working material. It lives in `testlab/` inside the checkout
# and is ignored here so it travels with the working copy but never lands in a
# commit. Docs that ARE committed stay English-only.
#
# `git clean -x` will delete an ignored `testlab/`; keep a copy elsewhere if a
# report matters. The loose `Pruefbericht*` / `testreport*` / `TESTLAB*`
# patterns are a belt-and-suspenders for a file drafted at the repo root by
# habit.
testlab/
Pruefbericht*
testreport*
TESTLAB*

# NOTE: config/server_info.conf is deliberately NOT ignored — it ships as a
# tracked template with placeholder values that SERVERINSTALL step 7 tells the
# operator to edit. Because it stays tracked, ignoring it here would have no
# effect anyway. Just do not commit your own server's name, location and
# contact address back to a fork.
